  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2025/01/12/handbrake-cli.html">handbrake cli</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2025-01-12">12 January 2025</time></p>
    <p>Handbrake is a compression program for multimedia. I use it to compress videos.</p>

<p>Handbrake has a CLI. Here’s my script.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>#!/bin/bash
echo "Format $0 input.mp4 output.mp4"
if [ -z "$input" ] || [ -z "$output" ]; then
  if [ "$#" -eq 2 ]; then
     input=$1
     output=$2
  else
     read -p "inputFile  : " $input
     read -p "outputFile : " $output 
  fi
fi
HandBrakeCLI -i $input -o $output -e x265 -Z "Very Fast 1080p30"
</code></pre></div></div>

  </article>

  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2025/01/10/bash-script-that-exits-if-previous-command-failed.html">bash script that exits if previous command failed</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2025-01-10">10 January 2025</time></p>
    <p>Here’s a bit of bash code that will exit if the previous command failed.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>#!/bin/bash
ls /nonexistentdirectory
if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
  echo "Previous command failed. Exiting."
  exit 1
fi
</code></pre></div></div>

