<p>Every variable in Bash is global and are accessible anywhere in the script.</p>

<p>They can be used in a function, loop, or conditional statement within the script.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code># setting a variable
a = "hello"
# printing a variable
echo $a
# using a variable inside a function
hello_function () {
