  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2023/06/18/date-from-a-year-ago.html">date from a year ago</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2023-06-18">18 June 2023</time></p>
    <p>Here’s a handy little script that has multiple applications to calculate date from a year ago.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>#!/bin/bash
now=$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
# mac os
year_old=$(date -v-1y +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S) 
# linux os 
year_old=$(date -d "-1 year" +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)
echo $now
echo $year_old
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Mac Os and Linux has slightly different formats. Pick one based on your OS.</p>

<p>Results</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>20230618-084940
20220618-084940
</code></pre></div></div>

