  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2020/03/31/aws-xfs-volume-setup.html">aws xfs volume setup</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2020-03-31">31 March 2020</time></p>
    <p>Here’s how to setup a XFS volume.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>file -s /dev/nvme2n1
mkfs -t xfs /dev/nvme2n1
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Mount to /data.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>mkdir /data
mount /dev/nvme2n1 /data
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Add to /etc/fstab.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>vim /etc/fstab
#
#
UUID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx /data  xfs  defaults 0 0
</code></pre></div></div>

  </article>

  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2020/03/28/create-swap-disk.html">create swap disk</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2020-03-28">28 March 2020</time></p>
    <p>To see which disk is available for swap disk use.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>lsblk
blkid
df -Th
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Format the disk.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>fdisk /dev/xvda
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Create a swap disk.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>sudo mkswap -f /dev/xvda
sudo swapon -s /dev/xvda
# or
sudo swapon /dev/xvda
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Check if swap disk is available.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>lsblk
free -h 
cat /proc/swaps
cat /proc/meminfo
swapon -s
top
vmstat
vmstat 1 5
</code></pre></div></div>

  </article>

