  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2020/01/26/bash-convert-bytes.html">bash convert bytes</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2020-01-26">26 January 2020</time></p>
    <p>Here’s a function to convert bytes into kilo, mega, giga, tera up to zeta bytes.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>function convert_bytes {
    bytes=$credits
    b=${bytes:-0}; d=''; s=0; S=(Bytes {K,M,G,T,E,P,Y,Z}B)
    while ((b &gt; 1024)); do
        d="$(printf ".%02d" $((b % 1000 * 100 / 1000)))"
        b=$((b / 1000))
        let s++
    done
    echo "$b$d ${S[$s]}"
}
credits=2308974418330
echo $credits 
convert_bytes $credits
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Result is:</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>2308974418330
2.30 TB
</code></pre></div></div>

  </article>

