    <p><time datetime="2020-01-21">21 January 2020</time></p>
    <p>Here’s how to determine what type of USB format a thumb drive is in Linux.</p>

<ul>
  <li>df -Th (shows the file system type)</li>
  <li>lsblk (shows the block devices)</li>
  <li>lsusb (show usb ports and devices)</li>
  <li>fdisk -l (displays the USB format type)</li>
</ul>

<p>To display, use “fdisk -l” to display either NTFS, FAT32 or exFAT32.</p>

