    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2019/08/31/remove-key-from-known_hosts.html">remove key from known_hosts</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2019-08-31">31 August 2019</time></p>
    <p>If you’ve changed keys, you will need to delete a ssh key from /etc/known_hosts file.</p>

<p>You can edit it manually using an editor such as vi or vim.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>vim ~/.ssh/known_hosts
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Or you can use ssh-keygen command with -R option to delete the hostname or IP address.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>ssh-keygen -f "~/.ssh/known_hosts" -R "xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx"
</code></pre></div></div>

