  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2019/07/25/aws-ec2-enable-secondary-ips.html">aws ec2 enable secondary ips</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2019-07-25">25 July 2019</time></p>
    <p>Here’s how to enable secondary private IPs for AWS EC2 instances.</p>

<ol>
  <li>Add secondary private IPs to the instance.
    <ul>
      <li>Editing the instance Networking &gt; Manage IP Addresses.</li>
      <li>Add new private IP addresses.</li>
      <li>Save.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li>Set the route configuration for each secondary IP address.
    <ul>
      <li>Config files are ifcfg-eth0:0, ifcfg-eth:0.1 and so on.</li>
      <li>Test each interface or IP to see if they respond to ping.</li>
      <li>/etc/sysconfig/network-scripts/</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ol>

<p>ifcfg-eth0:0</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>NM_CONTROLLED="no"
DEVICE="eth0:0"
ONBOOT="yes"
BOOTPROTO="static"
IPADDR="10.0.0.14"
NETMASK="255.255.255.255"
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>ifcfg-eth0:1</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>NM_CONTROLLED="no"
DEVICE="eth0:1"
ONBOOT="yes"
BOOTPROTO="static"
IPADDR="10.0.0.15"
NETMASK="255.255.255.255"
</code></pre></div></div>

  </article>

