    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2019/05/01/add-nofail.html">add nofail</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2019-05-01">01 May 2019</time></p>
    <p>The /etc/fstab file allow volumes to be automatically mounted on bootup. Add nofail in your automated mounts to prevent instances from hanging on boot. Nofail makes the instance to boot even if there are errors with the mounted volume.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>UUID=aebf131c-6957-451e-8d34-ec978d9581ae  /data  xfs  defaults,nofail  0  2
</code></pre></div></div>

