  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2019/02/24/aws-cli-efs-describe-file-systems.html">aws cli efs describe file systems</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2019-02-24">24 February 2019</time></p>
    <p>Show a list of EFS file systems within a region.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>aws efs describe-file-systems \
--region us-east-1
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>Filter by Name and FileSystemId.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>aws efs describe-file-systems \
--query 'FileSystems[*].[Name,FileSystemId]'
</code></pre></div></div>

  </article>

  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2019/02/20/rpm-check-packages.html">rpm check packages</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2019-02-20">20 February 2019</time></p>
    <p>How to check RPM if packages are installed.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>rpm -qa --last 
rpm -qa --last | more
rpm -qa --last | grep "package name"
</code></pre></div></div>

  </article>

  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2019/02/19/yum-remove-repo.html">yum remove repo</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2019-02-19">19 February 2019</time></p>
    <p>How to remove repos in Yum. Just delete the repo file in /etc/yum.repos.d.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>rm /etc/yum.repos.d/repo-name.repo
</code></pre></div></div>

