    <p>Looking for a text editor for editing code? Check out <a href="https://www.sublimetext.com/">Sublime Text 3</a>. You can install the text editor using several package managers depending on your Linux distro. There’s apt, yum, zypper, pacman and dnf. Here’s the Apt install of Sublime Text 3.</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>echo "deb https://download.sublimetext.com/ apt/stable/" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/sublime-text.list
