  <article>
    <h2 class="post-title"><a href="/2019/01/15/reset-locked-out-linux-user.html">reset locked out linux user</a></h2>
    <p><time datetime="2019-01-15">15 January 2019</time></p>
    <p>Perform this command to reset a Linux account that has been locked out due to multiple login failures. This involves resetting the pam_tally back down to zero. Some systems use pam_tally2. First, check what’s the current tally.</p>

<p>Current tally:</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>pam_tally --user=username
pam_tally2 --user=username
</code></pre></div></div>

<p>To reset:</p>

<div class="language-plaintext highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>pam_tally --user=username --reset
pam_tally2 --user=username --reset
</code></pre></div></div>

  </article>

